y ocean animal into a peaceful blue scene. Do not turn every wildlife tattoo into flowers surrounding an animal head. ROTATE SPECIES AGGRESSIVELY. Include familiar animals. Lion. Lioness. Tiger. Leopard. Jaguar. Panther. Wolf. Fox. Coyote. Bear. Polar bear. Elephant. Gorilla. Orangutan. Rhinoceros. Giraffe. Zebra. Stag. Moose. Bison. Ram. Mountain goat. Wild horse. Wild boar. But do not allow familiar animals to consume the category. Explore birds. Raven. Crow. Eagle. Falcon. Owl. Heron. Crane. Pelican. Flamingo. Hummingbird. Vulture. Peacock. Bat. Explore ocean life. Great white shark. Hammerhead shark. Whale. Orca. Dolphin. Manta ray. Octopus. Squid. Jellyfish. Sea turtle. Seahorse. Deep-sea animals. Explore reptiles and amphibians. Crocodile. Alligator. Cobra. Python. Rattlesnake. Chameleon. Iguana. Komodo dragon. Tortoise. Frog. Salamander. Explore strange and overlooked animals. Pangolin. Axolotl. Praying mantis. Beetles. Cicadas. Spiders. Scorpions. Centipedes. Rare regional wildlife. Explore prehistoric animals when appropriate. Treat them as animals rather than fantasy monsters. Use current scientific understanding when anatomical credibility matters. THE STYLE IS NOT FIXED. Use the full world of tattooing. Realism. Black and Grey Realism. Colour Realism. Fine Line. Sketch. Dotwork. Blackwork. Watercolour. Illustrative. Geometric. Japanese. American Traditional. Neo-Traditional. New School. Negative Space. Surrealism. And intelligent hybrids. Do not rotate styles mechanically. Ask what the animal gives the artist. Fur can become brushwork. Feathers can become Blackwork. Scales can become geometry. Spots can become Dotwork. Stripes can become abstraction. Tentacles can become body flow. Wings can become large negative-space compositions. Shells and armor can become texture studies. Translucent animals can become Colour Realism and Watercolour. White animals can be created through untouched skin. Black animals can emerge from darkness. THE ANIMALS ANATOMY SHOU